<BaseLayout title="Splitting Water — Position 4" sidebar>
  <CourseSidebar slot="sidebar" active="splitting-water" />

  <h1>Splitting Water <span class="tag tag-intermediate">Intermediate · Position 4</span></h1>

  <p>Splitting Water moves the hands from the front to the sides of the body, palms facing down, like water parting. Imagine balloons floating on the water's surface beneath each hand, and you gently press down on them. This posture expands the energy pathways to both sides of the body, opening a broader energy field.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <h4>📺 BBC Reference</h4>
    <p>《Stand Still Be Fit》Days 7-8: Splitting Water instruction and deepening</p>
  </div>

  ---

  <h2>Practice Guide</h2>
  <ul class="key-points">
    <li>Raise both hands from the sides of the body, palms down, elbows slightly bent</li>
    <li>Hands slightly below shoulder height, naturally positioned at the sides</li>
    <li>Not too far forward and not too far back</li>
    <li>Imagine two balloons floating on the water's surface beneath each hand — gently press down to keep them from escaping</li>
    <li>Imagine small balloons under the armpits supporting the arms</li>
    <li>Imagine sitting on a balloon chair (sitting-not-sitting), center of gravity stable</li>
    <li>Head suspended, shoulders relaxed, no puffing the belly</li>
  </ul>

  ---

  <h2>BBC Video: Day 7</h2>
  <p>The seventh episode teaches Splitting Water by a mountain stream. Philosophy theme: "the highest good is like water." The new warm-up "Side Shake Exhale" clears stale energy.</p>
  <VideoEmbed videoId="zhK0CH8TJiQ" title="Stand Still Be Fit - Day 7" />

